# Swift practice

- Swift 6, structured concurrency, `MainActor` for UI and session state.
- Mark CPU / AX / audio work `nonisolated` and hop to MainActor only on real UI deltas.
- No force-unwraps or `try!` in product paths. Use `guard`, `throws`, or typed results.
- Protocols at real boundaries (`SpeechTranscribing`, listen sources). Do not protocol-wrap every struct.
- SwiftData for conversations; Keychain for the API key; UserDefaults for lightweight prefs.
- Windows are AppKit (`NSPanel`). SwiftUI is the content, not the window policy.
- Prefer value types for catalogs, pricing, VAD, caption merge, and cursor math so they stay unit-testable.

```swift
// BAD
let key = settings.apiKey!

// GOOD
guard let key = try await keychain.load(), !key.isEmpty else { throw ChatError.missingAPIKey }
```
